Make a stash; it looks like you may not have one. Gold, spellbooks, 
potions, scrolls, and anything heavy you don't need on short notice go 
in the stash. I usually only carry a few things in the bag: holy water, 
certain wands (cancel always go in a special sack, and sacks never go in 
bags), a little spare food, useful rings, certain scrolls (taming, fire, 
rem curse).

You know you can recharge magic markers? You should get more than 3 
total scrolls from one. For wishes, wish up another (or two) and get 
your armor up to +4 or +5. Boost the saber too if you really intend to 
use it (not a good idea).

Get an intrinsic source of fire resistance, some way to levitate, and a 
better helm. I'd wear a different amulet (life saving is good for the 
first time) if you have one. Bless the worn equipment.

You should really push your level up as high as you can (probably won't 
reach 30, unless you've got foocubi handy); at this point, you're not 
really keeping the monsters easier, and the higher experience reduces 
spell failure, increases HP and power, and boosts spell damage. In any 
case, you need more HP.

Basically, if you were a very experienced player, you MIGHT be set to go 
for it. For the first time, be overprepared. Much of the stuff you want 
can be found in Gehennom but I'd be hesitant to enter with such low HP.

